# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Only read by the CLI (`vercel deploy`), which tars the working directory and
# sends it to the build machine — a git-connected deploy sends the commit
# instead and ignores this file. Everything below is either build OUTPUT, a
# local authoring workspace, or a second project that happens to live here; none
# of it is an input to `pnpm build`, and together they are most of the folder.
#
# The build itself decides what SHIPS (vite.config.ts `copyRuntimeArt` filters
# `assets/` on the way into dist) — this only decides what gets sent.

node_modules
.git

# Build output — Vercel builds its own.
dist
dist-*
test-results
test-results-*
playwright-report
.playwright-mcp

# The map editor's project store: 30 MB of embedded map art, reachable only
# through the dev server's `/__asset3d` middleware, which does not exist in a
# deploy. The game runs from src/data/zones.json, which is generated from it.
asset3d

# Authoring workspaces and neighbouring projects that carry their own git.
#
# NOT `assets/raw` — it looks like a workspace and mostly is, but the build
# SHIPS `raw/screamingbrain` from it (vite.config.ts `RAW_SHIPPED`) and
# assets.json references `raw/ai`. What is tracked here is 8 MB; the 3.9 GB of
# masters the .gitignore talks about lives in another checkout.
embergames
path-of-embers
rigger
world
tools/mapmask/out
agent-to-agent
.claude/worktrees

# Loose working files at the repo root.
*.zip
green_loop
*.log
bug-log.md
